<title>NORWAY: Aker wins Azerbaijan offshore contract.</title>
<headline>Aker wins Azerbaijan offshore contract.</headline>
<dateline>STAVANGER, Norway 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aker Rauma Offshore of Finland has won a 30 million crown contract to construct the 1,000 tonne module support frame for Azerbaijan Operating Co's Chirag 1 development in the Caspian Sea, Aker ASA said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The scope of the work includes detailed design, purchase of materials and construction.</p>
<p>Detailed design, plate-girder manufacturing and other prefabrication work will be carried out in Finland. Node fabrication, assembly and outfitting will be done in Baku, Azerbaijan.</p>
<p>The support frame is due for delivery in April 1997.</p>
</text>
